<title>USA: Colonial buys Georgia shopping center.</title>
<headline>Colonial buys Georgia shopping center.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colonial Properties Trust on Thursday said it bought a 336,000-square-foot shopping center in Athens, Georgia, for $22.2 million.</p>
<p>The purchase of Beechwood Shopping Center from Beechwood Associates, a group of local developers, was financed through the assumption of $11.9 million in debt, and an advance on Colonial's unsecured line of credit, the company said.</p>
<p>The acquisition increases Colonial's retail portfolio to 6.4 million square feet of shopping space in Alabama, Florida, Georgia and South Carolina.</p>
</text>
